obj['description']='Positive recurrence for the literal six-rate deterministic-first-chunk chain at every fixed positive arrival rate, with no aggregate cap on seed upload capacity.'
obj['plain_language']=['Imagine a file split into two pieces. Each arriving participant independently chooses at random which piece to fetch first and keeps that first choice. Participants leave as soon as both pieces are obtained, while one permanent seed always has both pieces.','The paper proves stability for a particular continuous-time random model at every fixed positive arrival rate. Stability here means positive recurrence and a unique stationary probability distribution. It does not imply a bound on average population or download time.','The exact model matters: empty participants are excluded from the contact denominator, and the permanent seed has no separate aggregate upload cap. Many empty participants can contact it at once. This result is not a stability theorem for a capped-seed model.','The associated large-system differential equations can have trajectories growing without bound. For this model, that behavior does not force instability of the random chain. The paper extends the elementary small-load argument to every fixed positive load.']
obj['result']=['For every fixed real λ>0, Theorem 1 states that the continuous-time chain on N₀⁴ is nonexplosive, irreducible and positive recurrent, and therefore has a unique stationary probability distribution. The conclusion covers every finite initial state.','The state (a,b,x,y) records empty participants assigned to each first-chunk choice and participants holding only each respective chunk. With D=x+y+1, the two arrivals have rate λ/2, the first downloads have rates a(x+1)/D and b(y+1)/D, and departures have rates x(y+1)/D and y(x+1)/D. A transition decrementing a zero coordinate has rate zero.','The seed contributes the +1 terms. The empty populations a and b do not enter D, and these rates allow unbounded aggregate seed upload as the waiting populations grow. The theorem applies to this literal generator.']
obj['limitations']=['The model has exactly two chunks, one permanent seed, independently uniform fixed first choices, immediate departure on completion and empty waiting rooms excluded from the contact denominator. It does not cover arbitrary file-sharing software or other chunk-selection rules.','The six rates impose no fixed aggregate seed-capacity bound. This is not a solution for a capped-seed or finite-bandwidth missing-piece model.','The arrival rate is fixed and strictly positive, and the proof constants can depend on it. No bound uniform in λ, stationary population moment, completion-time estimate, convergence rate or geometric ergodicity is established. At λ=0 the zero state is absorbing and the stated irreducibility conclusion does not apply.','The historical target is the 2010 Oberwolfach stability conjecture and the retained 2011 author-proof model. The 2009 preprint conjectured high-load instability instead. These source versions must be distinguished.','The classical Foster–Lyapunov method and finite birth–death Poisson equation are prior tools. The paper claims the all-load pointwise certificate for this model, and does not certify worldwide priority or continued openness.']
obj['status']='Unrefereed preprint draft, Zenodo version 1.0, dated 20 October 2026. Developed with extensive AI assistance; no completed independent human peer review or proof-assistant certification is claimed.'
